@startuml github-call-deadline
' cumin works - every call of the GitHub client ends after a deadline,
' a read that fails for a reason that passes is sent again, and no call
' leaves before the reset time of a full primary rate limit or during the
' wait of a secondary rate limit.
' Document: cumin-core.md, topic on the GitHub client.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

rectangle "cumin run\n(poll, actions)" as run
rectangle "cumin status" as status
rectangle "cumin setup" as setup
rectangle "AppClient\ninternal/platform/github\nREST and GraphQL" as client
cloud "GitHub API" as api

run --> client
status --> client
setup --> client
client -[#red,bold]-> api : <color:red>every try ends\n<color:red>after 30 seconds</color>

note right of client
  A try that gets no answer
  ends with an error at the deadline.
  A read (GET, GraphQL query) that fails
  with a network error or a 5xx answer
  is sent again: up to 3 retries,
  2 seconds apart, one warn log line each.
  A write is sent once.
  After the last try, the error
  is a temporary error (IsTemporary).
end note

note left of client
  An answer of a full primary rate limit
  (REST: 403 or 429, GraphQL: 200 with an error,
  both with x-ratelimit-remaining: 0)
  returns a RateLimitError with the reset time
  of x-ratelimit-reset, and one warn log line.
  It is not sent again at once.
  Until the reset time, a call of the same
  installation returns that error
  and sends nothing.
end note

note bottom of client
  An answer of a secondary rate limit
  (REST: 403 or 429, GraphQL: 200 or 403,
  with a message "secondary rate limit"
  or the header retry-after)
  returns a RateLimitError at once,
  and one warn log line.
  The wait is retry-after, else 1 minute.
  During the wait, a call of the same
  installation returns that error
  and sends nothing.
end note
@enduml
